Package Update Test Suite

Package Update Test Suite is framework for testing of package install/update.
This test suite verifies whether PackageManagerService can manage installed applications and
user data correctly through SW update (ROM1 -> ROM2).

Background:
- PackageManagerService is huge and complicated.
- Bugs in PackageManagerService cause serious problems on market.
- To maintain PackageManagerService securely, automated test is thought to be needed.

How to use it:

[Prerequisite]
- Ubuntu PC is required.
  - Test execution has been verified on Ubuntu14.
  - Add udev rule into /etc/udev/rules.d/51-android.rules for detecting target device by fastboot.
    see: https://developer.android.com/studio/run/device.html
  - Change sudo password timeout longer than the default.
    - $ sudo visudo
    - set timestamp_timeout=60 for example.
- Pixel / Pixel 2 are available with bootloader unlocked fully.
- Latest fastboot
- Download ROM images
  Need to place 2 version ROM for simulating letter update
  ex:ROM
      + -- radio.img
      + -- bootloader.img
      + -- aosp_walleye-img-xxxx-zip
- Build Android code
    - see: https://source.android.com/setup/build/building

[Run test]
 1. Move to root directory of source tree
 2. $ source ./build/envsetup.sh
 3. $ lunch <device-target>
 4. Create test applications
    $ make package_update-testapps
    NOTE:
      Build test applications and create zip archive in
        out/host/linux-x86/framework/PackageUpdate/testapps/testapps.zip

 5. $ make package_update-all
 6. Copy sources under frameworks/base/tests/PackageUpdate/harnesses/tradefed/ to tools/tradefederation/core/prod-tests.
    $ mkdir -p tools/tradefederation/core/prod-tests/res/config/pkgup
    $ cp frameworks/base/tests/PackageUpdate/harnesses/tradefed/config/* tools/tradefederation/core/prod-tests/res/config/pkgup/
    $ mkdir -p tools/tradefederation/core/prod-tests/src/com/android/tests/pkgup
    $ cp frameworks/base/tests/PackageUpdate/harnesses/tradefed/src/com/android/tests/pkgup/* tools/tradefederation/core/prod-tests/src/com/android/tests/pkgup/
 7. $ make tradefed-all
 8. $ cd out/host/linux-x86/framework/PackageUpdate/
 9. $ sudo echo
10. $ tradefed.sh
11. $ tf >run pkgup/basic-scope --rom1-zip <path/to/the/rom_1st> --rom2-zip <path/to/the/rom_2nd>


[Test result]
- When all tests are executed, logs and results are placed in out/host/linux-x86/framework/PackageUpdate/inv_<integer value>/.
    - Test summary is included in test_result_<integer value>.zip.
- The detailed test results are reported in out/host/linux-x86/framework/PackageUpdate/reports/html/analysis.html.


[Cleanup]
- If you want to reset the test environment, please execute folloing command.
    - $ make package_update-clean

